# Line endings. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check scripts out with CRLF:
# POSIX sh then stops at "set -eu\r" (Termux, iSH), and a release built from that clone ships them so.
# Everything that sh, Python or Node reads keeps LF on every checkout.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
launchers/*.sh text eol=lf
# PowerShell 5.1 and 7 read LF and CRLF alike; scripts/ps1_lint.py only requires one style per file.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
# The vendored Tokkio tree is declared unmodified (vendor/VENDOR.md lists every file's sha256): no
# line-ending conversion at all, whatever core.autocrlf says.
vendor/** -text
dist/*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
